# =============================================================================
# IqraSpace — apps/learning/.env.local.example
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (same folder) and fill in real values.
# `.env.local` is gitignored — never commit it. This example file IS committed
# and must only ever contain placeholders, no real secrets.
#
# HOW THIS PROJECT'S CONFIG FLOWS (read this before editing):
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars -> bundled into the browser by Next.js at build time.
#      Read automatically from this file by `npm run dev` / `npm run build`.
#   2. The backend is the iqraspace-learning Cloudflare Worker (worker/api):
#      D1 (database), R2 (lesson files) and a Durable Object (live lessons).
#      Its bindings live in wrangler.jsonc — it needs NO secrets, and nothing
#      in this file is read by the deployed Worker. See BACKEND.md.
#   3. The local scripts (seed:admins, seed:surah-lessons) read the values
#      below via `node --env-file=.env.local` and write to D1 through wrangler.
#
# Roles: tutor/student/guardian (ordinary accounts, via /signup) plus
# admin/super_admin (platform oversight — never grantable via signup; see
# the "Super Admin" section below).
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# Application
# =============================================================================

# Local base URL of this Next.js app. Not read by app code (routing is
# relative); used as Google's OAuth redirect base. Optional.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Free-text label, not read by any code. Optional.
APP_ENV=local

# Where the browser reaches the Learning API. Leave UNSET for production
# builds (it defaults to "<basePath>/api", i.e. /learning/api on the same
# origin). For local dev, run the API with `npm run dev:api` (wrangler dev on
# :8787, local D1/R2) next to `npm run dev`, and point the UI at it:
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8787/learning/api

# Base URL of apps/quran (the "Open Quran" / "Read in Quran" links — see
# lib/quranLink.ts). Optional: defaults to https://iqraspace.org/quran, which
# is NOT correct for local dev. Uncomment and run `npm run quran:dev` (from
# the repo root) alongside this app to test those links locally:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_QURAN_URL=http://localhost:3001

# =============================================================================
# Google Drive (optional, deferred feature)
# =============================================================================
# "Connect Google Drive" (architecture §8). Absent -> the Materials page
# correctly shows "not configured". The client ID is not secret. Note: the
# server-side token exchange was a never-deployed Supabase Edge Function
# (supabase/functions/google-oauth-exchange); it would need porting to the
# Worker before this feature can be turned on.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/materials

# =============================================================================
# Demo Accounts
# =============================================================================
# Ordinary tutor/student accounts, useful for manual testing. Passwords are
# never stored in the repo. Login is by USERNAME + password; these *_EMAIL
# vars are only a human-readable label for which account is which.
DEMO_TUTOR_EMAIL=
DEMO_TUTOR_PASSWORD=
DEMO_STUDENT_EMAIL=
DEMO_STUDENT_PASSWORD=

# =============================================================================
# Super Admin
# =============================================================================
# Roles live in users.role:
#   'admin'       — full management access across the entire app
#   'super_admin' — currently identical access to 'admin'
# Neither role is grantable through public signup — the only way to create
# one is:
#   npm run seed:admins               (local dev D1)
#   npm run seed:admins -- --remote   (production D1)
# which creates/updates the accounts "admin" and "superadmin" with the
# passwords below (see scripts/seed-admin-accounts.mjs). The *_EMAIL values
# are optional contact emails.
#
# GOTCHA: that script runs via `node --env-file=.env.local`, and Node's
# --env-file parser truncates a value at an unquoted `#`, mid-line — e.g.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=Foo#123 is silently read as just "Foo". Avoid `#`/`$` in
# these passwords, or wrap the value in double quotes: ADMIN_PASSWORD="Foo#123"
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-before-running-seed-admins
SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL=superadmin@example.com
SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-before-running-seed-admins

# =============================================================================
# One-time Supabase -> D1 data migration ONLY (delete after cutover)
# =============================================================================
# Read by scripts/migrate-from-supabase.mjs (npm run migrate:check / export /
# sql) — read-only access to the old Supabase project. Remove these, and
# delete the Supabase project, once production runs on D1. See BACKEND.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Notes
# =============================================================================
# - Lesson PDFs: private R2 bucket `iqraspace-learning`, bound to the Worker
#   as MATERIALS (wrangler.jsonc). No S3 keys needed anywhere.
# - In-app notifications are plain D1 rows; the app sends no email.
# - Cloudflare build (npm run build:cf): every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is baked in
#   at build time. None are required for production; `build:cf` sets
#   NEXT_BASE_PATH=/learning itself — do not put it here for local dev.
